- Prices and currencies are validated.
- Amounts use exact, consistent monetary representation.
- Offers preserve the required history.
- Counteroffers reference the appropriate job and offer.
- Accepted agreements reflect the authoritative backend state.
- Duplicate submissions are controlled.
- Concurrent acceptance attempts cannot produce conflicting accepted agreements.
- Stale offers are rejected correctly when the implemented rules require it.

Use transactions and database-level constraints where necessary.

Test conflicting requests rather than assuming that a button-disable state prevents race conditions.

Never display an unconfirmed offer acceptance as a completed agreement.

## 4.3 Geospatial matching and location privacy

